 "generatorWeaknesses": [
  "There is no dye verb (물들이다, 칠하다). Colouring is only expressible as CRAFT of a coloured item or as GIVE of a dye to a sheep, which prints 양에게 파란색 염료를 주세요 and reads as feeding. A step `염료로 양털을 물들이세요` (L2.euro_material) is impossible; CRAFT with `with` ingredients prints \"염료와 양털로 …를 만드세요\" but needs three unknown words at once.",
  "A colour word cannot be the taught word of a dyed item: teaching 빨간색 on red dye prints \"빨간색을 만드세요\" (the colour replaces the whole noun). And the concept 염료 owns minecraft:red_dye, so red dye can only be said as bare 염료; blue, orange and the others come from per-item gen_ concepts that must exist (gen_red_bed, gen_red_candle, gen_orange_tulip do not).",
  "A general word with covers swallows the colour: teaching 침대, 초, 양탄자, 양털 or 꽃 prints the plain word for every colour, so \"빨간색 침대\" cannot be asked together with the word 침대. Colour contrast therefore needs the gen_ concept or no teach of the general word, and then the colour compound is a single unknown token.",
  "The material of a PLACE_ON_PATTERN or the anchor is named with the general word only if the same step also teaches it (teach [flower, fence]); otherwise the full wood name appears (가문비나무 울타리), which is one more unknown word.",
  "The `gate` concept names only the oak gate, and the validator requires the first taught word to describe the goal. A spruce gate cannot be taught (teach the fence for the placing step, the verb 열다 for the opening step) and prints its full official name. HANG_DOOR oak_fence_gate is also at the pair limit of 3.",
  "Tiered armour does not mention its slot word: a leather cap prints 가죽 모자 while the taught concept is 투구, so the validator fails with \"clue omits the taught word\"; EQUIP on #minecraft:head_armor passes validation but has no status line and the playtest cannot drive it. The tannery therefore stores the cap in a chest instead of wearing it.",
  "Step signatures ignore count, station and `with`, so CRAFT map / item_frame / book and ACQUIRE lava_bucket / map collide with steps of earlier or later trails. Every clash counts as a duplicate for whichever trail comes second on the learner path, even when it is not one of mine (obstgarten, a strider trail, w9_02 became duplicates of my first drafts).",
  "Saturated (verb, object) pairs at the limit of 3 leave few objects for a garden or a treasure room: PLACE chest, barrel, furnace, crafting_table, flower_pot, lantern, torch, hay_block; STAND candle, oak_sign, spruce_sign; PLANT poppy, dandelion, cornflower; HANG_DOOR oak_fence_gate; CRAFT paper, bucket. I used birch, jungle, acacia and dark oak signs, coloured candles and tulips instead.",
  "The unknown-word budget is global: dropping an old step that said 여섯 개 made a BATCH-012 sentence (adv_adventure_salvage_sherd/finale) go over one unknown word. I put the count 6 into the chiseled bookshelf trail (six books fill the shelf) to keep the ratchet.",
  "A chiseled bookshelf has no front: IN_FRONT_OF is refused by the validator (the finale uses ON_TOP_OF). The playtest also could not satisfy a NEAR_BLOCK torch on a LOOK_AT_BLOCK finale after the torches were placed as BETWEEN anchors, so the treasure-room finale has no condition.",
  "SEQUENCE prints the object of both parts: craft boots then wear boots reads \"가죽 장화를 만들고 가죽 장화를 신으세요\". The tannery uses separate steps instead.",
  "The German giveaway check blocks the separable prefix \"auf\" (aufstellen, aufhängen) and \"nach\" (\"nach oben\") in relation and order clues, so the German verbs are platzieren / anbringen / hochklettern.",
  "보물, 정원 and 예쁘다 are not in the lexicon, so no generated or authored sentence uses them (the titles that contain them are kept). 칠하다 and 물들이다 are not supported either."
 ],
 "openIssues": [
  "Reachability in the first week: the gold block of the treasure room needs nine gold ingots; the coloured candles (farbenpfad, festungpfad) need honeycomb; the compass needs iron and redstone; the lava bucket needs an iron bucket and lava; a Y 40 descent needs a cave; the crafter needs five iron, redstone and a dropper. glueckspfad asks for gold ore, which is deep or in badlands. All are overworld and need no structure.",
  "adv_husbandry_obtain_netherite_hoe is now a garden-tool trail with a new title (괭이의 길 / The Hoe Trail) and leaves reachabilityDebt. The vanilla advancement name is gone from the journal; if the owner wants it back it needs a Nether trail at level 3.",
  "The dye-a-sheep steps (farbenpfad s1, faerberei s4) say 주세요 because GIVE is the only verb that fits (see the weakness above); a linguist may find it odd.",
  "farbenpfad and festungpfad ask for coloured candles; no colour of 보라색, 검은색, 하얀색, 회색, 갈색 appears in a clue because each would be a second unknown compound word on a sentence that already has one.",
  "No trail is proposed for level 3.",
  "BATCH-013 had not landed when I merged phase0 the last time (UI pass and the Spanish language came in). If it lands first, regenerate and re-read the generated lines; my trails use (verb, object) pairs that BATCH-013 (animals) should not need."
 ]
